<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="chick-not-pie" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Chicken Not Pie</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup olive oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 leeks, washed well, dried, and chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup dry white wine</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 cup vegetable stock</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon chopped fresh thyme or tarragon</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 boneless chicken breasts</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 large red potatoes, cut into 1-inch cubes</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium carrots, cut into coins</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> pound sugar snap peas, trimmed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> pound asparagus, cut into 1-inch pieces</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 tablespoons lemon juice</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Put half the oil in a large skillet on medium heat.  Add leeks, salt, and pepper, and cook for 5 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add wine, stock, and thyme, and boil 1 minute.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add chicken, reduce heat, cover, simmer till barely cooked (5 minutes), then remove.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add potatoes.  Bring to a boil, then simmer 5 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add carrots, and cook a few minutes.  The liquid should thicken (if not turn up heat and cook for a few minutes while stirring).
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Slowly add remaining oil while stirring.  Add peas and asparagus.  Cook for 3 minutes.  Chop chicken; return to skillet with any chicken juices and the lemon juice.  Warm through.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>